NOTE ON THIRD-PARTY DEPENDENCIES (not part of the MIT text above):

HybridEQ's own source code (everything in this repository) is released under
the MIT License above. This project is built on the JUCE framework
(https://juce.com), which is fetched at build time and not redistributed
here. JUCE is dual-licensed, and whoever compiles this code into a binary is
bound by their own JUCE license, independent of HybridEQ's MIT license:
  - If you hold a paid JUCE commercial license (Starter, Indie, Pro, or
    Educational), you may compile and distribute closed-source binaries
    under that license's terms (including its revenue/funding limits, where
    applicable).
  - If you do not hold a commercial JUCE license, JUCE's free tier requires
    your compiled binary to be licensed under the AGPLv3 instead.
This MIT license does not grant you a JUCE license of any kind — you must
hold your own valid JUCE license (commercial or AGPLv3) to legally
distribute anything you build from this source.

AAX (Pro Tools) BUILD TARGET: the AAX plug-in format requires Avid's
proprietary AAX SDK, which is provided under Avid's own developer
agreement/NDA and is NOT included in, or redistributed by, this
repository. Avid's terms are incompatible with GPL/AGPL-style source
disclosure requirements, and only developers formally approved and
PACE-code-signed through the Avid Developer Program can legally
distribute functional (non-"Developer build") AAX plugins. Building the
AAX target from this source is possible for personal/local use if you
separately obtain the AAX SDK yourself, but pre-built AAX binaries should
not be publicly redistributed from this project unless the distributor
holds their own valid Avid developer agreement.
